  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tajikistan: Commercial Mediation - Phase 3: COVID-19 Response: Support with Adoption of the Law on Mediation and Promotion of Commercial Mediation to Small- and Medium-Sized Enterprises (SMEs)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To enable the Working Group on Development of the Law on Mediation of the Republic of Tajikistan to finalize the draft and adopt the Law. 2) To carry out awareness-raising campaigns on the benefits of commercial mediation and to advance the legislative drafting process of the draft Law.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Ministry of Justice, Office of the Commissioner for Human Rights in the Republic of Tajikistan, Presidential Administration of Tajikistan, Supreme Economic Court (SEC), Supreme Court (SC), Commercial Mediation Centre (CMC) under the Chamber of Commerce, Industry of the Republic of Tajikistan (CCI), Working Group on Development of the Law on Mediation, mediators, and law, business, banking and insurance associations, Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SME) Finance &amp; Development Team (ASB team) and SME clients. Indirect beneficiaries: Wider business community in Tajikistan.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimed to assist the Government of the Republic of Tajikistan with the adoption of the Law on Mediation and the promotion and facilitation of the use of commercial mediation among small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) to make the use of mediation, including online mediation, a business norm in the Republic of Tajikistan.</narrative>
  </description>
